But how to confirm this? The user might need to check the image's contents. Since they can't do that directly, maybe they can check the deployment's YAML to see the command and image details. Using kubectl to get the deployment's YAML would help. So the next step is to retrieve the deployment configuration for the frontend service to check the image and command specified. That way, they can verify if the image is correct and if the command is properly set to run the frontend executable.
